 ISDN was primarily used for voice and fax traffic. Until 2007 ISDN (BRI) and ADSL/VDSL were often bundled on the same line, mainly because the combination of ADSL\n\n[Passage 3]\npassage_id: atlas-dpr-wikipedia:000000200516\ntitle: Integrated Services Digital Network\ntext: to retire the UK's ISDN infrastructure by 2025. France Telecom offers ISDN services under their product name Numeris (2 B+D), of which a professional Duo and home Itoo version is available. ISDN is generally known as RNIS in France and has widespread availability. The introduction of ADSL is reducing ISDN use for data transfer and Internet access, although it is still common in more rural and outlying areas, and for applications such as business voice and point-of-sale terminals. In Germany, ISDN was very popular with an installed base of 25 million channels (29% of all subscriber lines in Germany as\n\n[Passage 4]\npassage_id: atlas-dpr-wikipedia:000002032703\ntitle: ISDN digital subscriber line\ntext: fees by being generally billed at a flat-rate. IDSL is not available in all countries. ISDN digital subscriber line (IDSL) is a cross between ISDN and xDSL. It is like ISDN in that it uses a single-wire pair to transmit full-duplex data at 128 kbit/s and at distances of up to RRD range. Like ISDN, IDSL uses a 2B1Q line code to enable transparent operation through the ISDN U interface. Finally, the user continues to use existing CPE (ISDN BRI terminal adapters, bridges, and routers) to make the CO connections. The big difference is from the carrier's point of view.\n\n[Passage 5]\npassage_id: atlas-dpr-wikipedia:000012795447\ntitle: Common ISDN Application Programming Interface\ntext: Common ISDN Application Programming Interface The Common ISDN Application Programming Interface (short CAPI) is an ISDN-conformant standardized software interface. With the help of the CAPI-Interface computer software intended for the use with ISDN can be provided, without knowledge of the deployed, proprietary ISDN card. CAPI was designed from 1989 by German manufacturers (AVM, Systec, Stollmann). Since 1991 CAPI is being developed further by \"CAPI Association e.V.\" Implementations exist for different operating systems, including Linux and Microsoft Windows. Through the ETSI CAPI 2.0 was introduced as standard ETS 300 324 (Profile B). Primarily CAPI was designed for data transfer over ISDN.","terminal_format_issue":"Format Agent is not selected as the Output Agent","topology_statistics":{"agent_count":0,"component_count":0,"directed_edge_count":0,"fan_in_agent_ids":[],"fan_out_agent_ids":[],"max_depth":0,"max_width":0,"output_agent_id":null,"quotient_directed_edge_count":0,"reciprocal_pair_count":0,"relation_count":0,"root_agent_ids":[],"root_component_count":0,"sink_agent_ids":[],"sink_component_count":0,"structural_depth":0,"topology_family":"empty","topology_motifs":[]}}","role":"user"},{"content":"{"action":"set_output","agent_id":"format"}","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Canvas observation. Choose exactly one next action using only the task, messages, Canvas, catalog, and any supplied validated Skill facts.

